From: Inferno RIO
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ssi/sx1276: say when the part can hear again

can_receive() returning false does not only drop the frame in hand.
qemu stops the peer's queue at that point and does not start it again
until somebody calls qemu_flush_queued_packets(); this model never
did.  A radio is deaf while it transmits, so the first time two
stations talk at once the queue stops -- and the link then carries
nothing at all, for ever, with no flag, no counter and no log line
anywhere to say why.

It is not a rare case.  Any protocol where both ends speak before
either has listened hits it immediately: keyring->auth() is one, and
it could not be run over this radio at all.  What the guest sees is a
receiver that stops for no reason it can name, which is where an
afternoon goes; two Inferno stations counted 21 frames out and 1 in
and both blamed their own driver.

Flush when the part enters a receiving mode, which is the only moment
at which the answer to can_receive() changes from false to true.

With this, keyring->auth() completes over two SX1276s on one socket:
12 frames each way, no retries, each end learning the other's
certified identity and deriving the same 128-byte secret.
---
diff --git a/hw/ssi/sx1276.c b/hw/ssi/sx1276.c
index c5a54f3..fefb50c 100644
--- a/hw/ssi/sx1276.c
+++ b/hw/ssi/sx1276.c
@@ -309,6 +309,22 @@ static void sx1276_set_opmode(SX1276State *s, uint8_t val)
         }
         sx1276_transmit(s);
     }
+
+    /*
+     * Tell the net layer the part can hear again.
+     *
+     * can_receive() returning false does not only drop the frame in
+     * hand: qemu stops the peer's queue and does not restart it until
+     * somebody flushes.  A radio is deaf while it transmits, so the
+     * first time two stations talk at once this happens -- and without
+     * this call the link never carries anything again.  The guest sees
+     * a receiver that stops for no reason it can name, which is where
+     * an afternoon goes.
+     */
+    if ((now == MODE_RXCONTINUOUS || now == MODE_RXSINGLE) &&
+        was != now && s->nic) {
+        qemu_flush_queued_packets(qemu_get_queue(s->nic));
+    }
 }
 
 static void sx1276_reg_write(SX1276State *s, uint8_t addr, uint8_t val)
